I stand in the mobile shop.
The shopkeeper gives me the new SIM card.
He looks at the computer.
He says, "The SIM is active now."
"Do you have a phone?"
I say, "Yes, I have a phone."
I put the SIM card in my phone.
The shopkeeper gives me a paper.
He asks, "Is the number correct?"
I look at the new number on the paper.
I read the number aloud.
"Nine, eight, seven, six, five."
"Four, three, two, one, zero."
The shopkeeper smiles.
He says, "Yes, the number is correct."
He asks, "Do you have a network signal now?"
I look at the phone.
I say, "Yes, I have a signal."
I give him three hundred rupees.
Now I have an Indian mobile number.
